„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections–…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ÷And it came to pass in the days of Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, king of Judah, that Rezin the king of Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah, king of Israel, went up toward Jerusalem to war against it, but could not prevail against it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And it was told the house of David, saying, Syria is confederate with Ephraim. And his heart was moved, and the heart of his people, as the trees of the wood are moved with the wind.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«Then said the LORD unto Isaiah, Go forth now to meet Ahaz, thou, and Shearjashub thy son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller's field;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁand say unto him, Take heed, and be quiet; fear not, neither be fainthearted for the two tails of these smoking firebrands, for the fierce anger of Rezin with Syria, and of the son of Remaliah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Because Syria, Ephraim, and the son of Remaliah, have taken evil counsel against thee, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Let us go up against Judah, and vex it, and let us make a breach therein for us, and set a king in the midst of it, even the son of Tabeal:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKthus saith the Lord GOD, It shall not stand, neither shall it come to pass.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœFor the head of Syria is Damascus, and the head of Damascus is Rezin; and within threescore and five years shall Ephraim be broken, that it be not a people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd the head of Ephraim is Samaria, and the head of Samaria is Remaliah's son. If